      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T21:00:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This MMI requires us to wait for a connection to be established by the PTS with the IUT. While returning just \"OK\" may work here, we probably want to implement a behavior similar to `TSC_AVDTP_mmi_iut_accept_connect` in the future:\n\n1/ We should wait for a connection to be established using the `self.host.WaitConnection` method.\n\n2/ Then, we should call a method waiting for the control channel to be established, which depends on the type of the test, similar to `WaitSink`/`WaitSource` for A2DP: if the test is CT, we should define a `WaitController` method in an `avrcp.proto` file that we should implement in the `Avrcp.kt` file. If the test is TG, we should define a `WaitTarget` method in a similar fashion.\n\nHowever since it\u0027s not needed right now, just add a `#TODO: Wait for connection to be established and AVCTP control channel to be open` before the `return`.",
